    "declared_Wilson_Maxwell_onsite_complement_energy_completion": "The changed Hamiltonian adds m c(g) times the sum of onsite-in-macrocell code-complement projectors, with c(g) equal to g squared times the stated source-derived dyadic coefficient. The choice of this positive completion is explicit; the unmodified source ground outside the occupation code and the completed coupled ground are distinct. All complements, original code energies, kinetic guards, reference costs and complete preparation filters are retained.",
