    "declared_local_gauge_invariant_current_pointer_coupling": "The apparatus adds an explicitly controlled finite neutral pointer coupling built from a local gauge-invariant polynomial of the actual dressed current. Admission flags, source evolution during the finite readout interval and all measurement errors and work bounds are retained. This is a declared narrower apparatus primitive; preparation and spectral-bin services retain their separate full-matrix premise, and no autonomous native-C/E implementation is inferred.",
    "declared_native_Wilson_Maxwell_cube_and_affine_Gauss_embedding": "The declared open-cube Wilson current is coupled to the five finite transverse modes through literal finite-cutoff Peierls exponentials and an exact longitudinal charge/reference embedding. Full native complement charges, the static compensator, the complete Gauss-orthogonal extension, the source-selected length/time scale and all cutoff boundary commutators are retained. This is an added finite source architecture, not a transfer from the scalar square-root kinetic source or an electromagnetic identification."
